.obsidian/workspace*.json
.obsidian/graph.json
.smart-env/
.trash/
.DS_Store
_WORK/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env*

# Everything Obsidian saves in System/Attachments — pasted images and photos, the
# Life OS Hub banners (banners/, old-banners/, "dark mode.*", "light mode.*") — is
# the user's own, often someone else's art, and must never be committed. Only the
# .gitkeep stays, so the folder exists on a fresh clone.
System/Attachments/*
!System/Attachments/.gitkeep

# Personal by nature: who you are, what you write, what you plan. The template
# ships John's sample files here (already tracked, so they stay tracked; a
# new file you create is not picked up, and `demo.py clear` drops what is left
# of John from the git index). `git add -f <file>` puts one in a PRIVATE repo,
# or delete the line. To add a demo file yourself: git add -f.
Life/roadmap/avatar.md
Life/roadmap/roadmap-brief.md
Life/roadmap/backlog.md
Life/roadmap/roadmap-brief.previous.md
Life/INBOX.md
Life/Journal/
Life/Notes/
Life/Patterns/observation-log.md
Life/Patterns/patterns.md

# Generated by System/scripts/vault-status.py (the Life OS Hub Status tab reads it).
System/status.json
System/runs.json
